    <string name="thermal_help_intro_title">How It Works</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_intro_body">Xiaomi thermal files in /vendor/etc/thermal-*.conf are encrypted with AES-128-CBC for mi_thermald. When you open a file here, it is automatically decrypted for editing. When you tap Save &amp; Apply, it is re-encrypted and applied as an override in /data/vendor/thermal/config/, and mi_thermald is restarted. Original stock files in /vendor/etc/ are never modified.</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_structure_title">File Structure</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_structure_body">Each section in [BRACKETS] defines a virtual sensor or a throttling rule:\n• algo_type: algorithm (ss = clock throttling, monitor = stepped actions, Virtual = combined sensor)\n• sensor: monitored sensor (usually VIRTUAL-SENSOR0 or battery)\n• device: controlled component (cpu0 = Little, cpu4 = Big, cpu7 = Prime, gpu, battery, lcd)\n• polling: check interval in milliseconds (1000 = 1 second)</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_temp_title">Adjusting Temperatures (trig &amp; clr)</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_temp_body">Temperatures are in millidegrees Celsius (m°C): 40000 = 40 °C, 45000 = 45 °C, 48000 = 48 °C.\n• trig: temperature at which the limit activates.\n• clr: temperature at which the limit clears (must always be lower than its matching trig).\n• Keep values in ascending order and make sure trig, clr, and target have the exact same number of columns separated by tabs.</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_clock_title">Adjusting Clocks &amp; Limits (target)</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_clock_body">• CPU (cpu0, cpu4, cpu7): frequencies in kHz (e.g. 1766400 = 1766 MHz, 2227200 = 2227 MHz). Always use valid frequencies supported by the cluster.\n• GPU (gpu): frequency or level matching the original format of that file.\n• Battery (battery): charging current limit levels (higher level = lower charging current).</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_safety_title">Safety Tips</string>
    <string name="thermal_help_safety_body">• Raise temperature thresholds gradually (2–3 °C at a time) and monitor battery temperature.\n• Never disable thermal protection completely — excessive heat can degrade the battery or cause thermal shutdown.\n• If anything behaves unexpectedly, tap Reset on the file (or Reset all overrides) to return immediately to stock.</string>
